; A near miss that must NOT collapse — the two arms are genuinely different logical values, so
; today's two-variant type-choice enum is retained.
;
; Mismatched occurrence bounds (`#6.258([+ uint]) / [* uint]`): the tagged arm requires >=1 element,
; the untagged arm allows empty, so the arms are not the same value and the collapse condition (arms
; equal but for one `Tagged` op, occurrence bounds INCLUDED) does not hold. The IR keeps a
; `TypeChoice`; the SURVIVING tagged arm is itself an inline `#6.258([+ uint])` occurrence, so it
; nominalizes to the shape-derived `SetNonEmptyU64` set wrapper (Phase 2.4), while the untagged arm
; stays a plain `Vec<u64>` variant — the union does not collapse, but its tagged arm gets set
; semantics exactly like any other inline 258 occurrence. The other
; near misses (different element types, both arms tagged, 3+ arms) are pinned in-process in
; `optional_tag_set_tests.rs`; this fixture locks that the retained enum still compiles and
; round-trips under every profile.
near_miss = #6.258([+ uint]) / [* uint]
holder = [x: near_miss]
